body:
### Summary

I'm setting up uv use in all python project teams for an administration.

When using uv-installer.sh or uv-installer.ps1, the resolution of the artifact download urls doesn't test for UV_ASTRAL_MIRROR_URL.

For instance in `uv-installer.ps1`:
```
if ($env:UV_DOWNLOAD_URL) {
  $ArtifactDownloadUrls = @($env:UV_DOWNLOAD_URL)
} elseif ($env:INSTALLER_DOWNLOAD_URL) {
  $ArtifactDownloadUrls = @($env:INSTALLER_DOWNLOAD_URL)
} elseif ($env:UV_INSTALLER_GHE_BASE_URL) {
  $installer_base_url = $env:UV_INSTALLER_GHE_BASE_URL
  $ArtifactDownloadUrls = @("$installer_base_url/astral-sh/uv/releases/download/0.12.23")
} elseif ($env:UV_INSTALLER_GITHUB_BASE_URL) {
  $installer_base_url = $env:UV_INSTALLER_GITHUB_BASE_URL
  $ArtifactDownloadUrls = @("$installer_base_url/astral-sh/uv/releases/download/0.12.23")
} else {
  $ArtifactDownloadUrls = @("https://releases.astral.sh/github/uv/releases/download/0.12.23", "https://github.com/astral-sh/uv/releases/download/0.12.23")
}
```

Other environment variables are tested, but they require:
- to know the exact installer path down to the version for UV_DOWNLOAD_URL & INSTALLER_DOWNLOAD_URL
- to have a mirror pointing to https://github.com for UV_INSTALLER_GHE_BASE_URL and UV_INSTALLER_GITHUB_BASE_URL

This is an issue for my organization because:
- we want to have an easy install and self update for all team members: knowing the exact installer path at all times is not easy for them
- Security team requires that components operate exclusively through proxy repositories, but also forbids a mirror pointing directly to https://github.com: UV_INSTALLER_GHE_BASE_URL and UV_INSTALLER_GITHUB_BASE_URL cannot work for us.
However, the security team is ok with a mirror pointing to https://releases.astral.sh: UV_ASTRAL_MIRROR_URL would be great for us.

My team would be happy to contribute with your approval: however, I cannot find the source code for the standalone installers.

### Platform

Linux 6.8.0-138-generic x86_64 GNU/Linux, Windows 11 x64

### Version

0.12.23

